## Goal
Make `scripts/build-app.sh` refuse any build directory located anywhere inside `~/Applications`, not only one equal to it. This follows a cross-review finding.

## Problems
None.

## Decision
The existing guard compared the resolved build directory only for equality with the resolved `~/Applications`. A directory nested inside it, such as inside the installed `Portero.app`, passed the check. `make install` would then delete or overwrite its own build or the installed app.

The check now also matches by prefix. It appends a trailing `/` to the resolved output path and uses a `case` pattern against `"$APPS"/*`. The trailing slash avoids false matches on sibling directories that share a name prefix. The check stays in POSIX `sh`, with no new dependencies. The error message now says "inside ~/Applications".

`scripts/test-install.sh` gets a regression case. It sets the build directory to a path under the installed app and asserts that `install.sh` fails. It also checks that the installed app's marker file is untouched. The success message was updated to match.

